1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,320
Two twelve inch pizzas or one eighteen

2
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:04,640
inch pizza? Which gives you more pizza?

3
00:00:04,640 --> 00:00:06,240
The eighteen inch wins.

4
00:00:06,240 --> 00:00:08,000
It has exactly twelve and a half percent

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,200
more surface area.

6
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:10,960
Engineers use the same geometry for the

7
00:00:10,960 --> 00:00:13,840
cross sections of pipes, wires and bolts.

8
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:16,000
Let's settle it with one formula you

9
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,120
already know.

10
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:19,120
Pizza sizes are diameters.

11
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:20,800
A twelve inch pizza is twelve inches

12
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:22,560
straight across, through the center.

13
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:24,560
But how much pizza you get depends on the

14
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:27,120
area: the whole pizza as seen from above,

15
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:28,400
including the crust.

16
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:30,400
And area does not grow the way the

17
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:31,840
diameter does.

18
00:00:31,840 --> 00:00:34,560
The area of a circle is pi r squared,

19
00:00:34,560 --> 00:00:37,120
where r is the radius, half the diameter.

20
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:39,200
A twelve inch pizza has a radius of six

21
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:41,390
inches. Six squared is thirty six, and

22
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:43,190
thirty six times pi is about one hundred

23
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:45,200
thirteen square inches.

24
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:47,280
Two of those pizzas give you seventy two

25
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:49,280
pi, about two hundred twenty six square

26
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:50,080
inches.

27
00:00:50,080 --> 00:00:51,280
Now the big one.

28
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:53,280
An eighteen inch pizza has a radius of

29
00:00:53,280 --> 00:00:55,520
nine inches. Nine squared is eighty one,

30
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:57,460
and eighty one times pi is about two

31
00:00:57,470 --> 00:00:59,670
hundred fifty four square inches.

32
00:00:59,670 --> 00:01:01,140
The two small pizzas together had two

33
00:01:01,150 --> 00:01:02,550
hundred twenty six.

34
00:01:02,550 --> 00:01:05,020
The single pizza wins by nine pi, about

35
00:01:05,030 --> 00:01:06,630
twenty eight square inches.

36
00:01:06,630 --> 00:01:08,870
Divide one by the other and pi cancels

37
00:01:08,870 --> 00:01:10,950
out. Eighty one over seventy two is

38
00:01:10,950 --> 00:01:12,950
exactly one point one two five.

39
00:01:12,950 --> 00:01:14,470
That's twelve and a half percent more

40
00:01:14,470 --> 00:01:17,190
surface area, in one box instead of two.

41
00:01:17,190 --> 00:01:18,550
Here's the real reason.

42
00:01:18,550 --> 00:01:21,110
Write the area with the diameter d

43
00:01:21,110 --> 00:01:23,990
instead. It's pi d squared over four.

44
00:01:23,990 --> 00:01:25,830
The diameter is squared.

45
00:01:25,830 --> 00:01:27,990
An eighteen inch pizza is one and a half

46
00:01:27,990 --> 00:01:29,910
times as wide as a twelve inch.

47
00:01:29,910 --> 00:01:31,680
But one and a half squared is two point

48
00:01:31,690 --> 00:01:35,430
two five. So one eighteen inch pizza has

49
00:01:35,430 --> 00:01:37,670
two and a quarter times the area of one

50
00:01:37,750 --> 00:01:40,070
twelve inch pizza, not one and a half

51
00:01:40,070 --> 00:01:42,070
times. To see how much pizza you're

52
00:01:42,070 --> 00:01:44,070
getting, compare the areas.

53
00:01:44,070 --> 00:01:45,590
Here's the whole picture.

54
00:01:45,590 --> 00:01:48,230
This curve is pizza area against diameter.

55
00:01:48,230 --> 00:01:50,630
It bends upward because of that square.

56
00:01:50,630 --> 00:01:52,540
A twelve inch pizza sits here, at one

57
00:01:52,550 --> 00:01:53,910
hundred thirteen.

58
00:01:53,910 --> 00:01:56,310
The dashed line is two twelve inch pizzas,

59
00:01:56,310 --> 00:01:57,430
at two hundred twenty six.

60
00:01:57,820 --> 00:02:00,220
The curve crosses it just under seventeen

61
00:02:00,300 --> 00:02:02,540
inches. Every pizza bigger than that beats

62
00:02:02,540 --> 00:02:04,220
the pair, and the eighteen inch sits

63
00:02:04,220 --> 00:02:05,330
clearly above it, at two hundred fifty

64
00:02:05,340 --> 00:02:07,180
four and a half.

65
00:02:07,420 --> 00:02:09,580
Where exactly is that crossing?

66
00:02:09,580 --> 00:02:12,060
Set one pizza's area equal to two twelve

67
00:02:12,060 --> 00:02:14,700
inch pizzas. The pi cancels, and you get d

68
00:02:14,860 --> 00:02:17,100
squared equals two hundred eighty eight.

69
00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:19,820
So d is twelve times the square root of

70
00:02:19,820 --> 00:02:21,850
two. The break even point is about sixteen

71
00:02:21,860 --> 00:02:23,980
point nine seven inches.

72
00:02:23,980 --> 00:02:26,460
A seventeen inch pizza is just barely

73
00:02:26,460 --> 00:02:27,740
larger than the pair.

74
00:02:27,740 --> 00:02:29,650
A sixteen inch pizza, at about two hundred

75
00:02:29,660 --> 00:02:32,380
one square inches, still loses.

76
00:02:32,380 --> 00:02:34,060
Here are common sizes.

77
00:02:34,060 --> 00:02:36,140
A ten inch pizza is about seventy nine

78
00:02:36,300 --> 00:02:37,260
square inches.

79
00:02:37,260 --> 00:02:39,740
A twelve inch is one hundred thirteen.

80
00:02:39,740 --> 00:02:42,380
A fourteen inch has almost twice the area

81
00:02:42,380 --> 00:02:43,580
of the ten inch.

82
00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:45,740
Just four more inches across, and nearly

83
00:02:45,740 --> 00:02:47,340
double the surface area.

84
00:02:47,340 --> 00:02:49,580
A sixteen inch has more than two and a

85
00:02:49,580 --> 00:02:51,660
half times the area of the ten inch.

86
00:02:51,660 --> 00:02:54,060
And an eighteen inch has over three times

87
00:02:54,060 --> 00:02:55,740
the area of the ten inch.

88
00:02:55,740 --> 00:02:57,580
For pizzas of similar thickness and

89
00:02:57,580 --> 00:02:59,900
toppings, area is a fair estimate of how

90
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:01,100
much food you get.

91
00:03:01,150 --> 00:03:03,230
This is also how to compare prices.

92
00:03:03,390 --> 00:03:05,550
Divide the price by the area.

93
00:03:05,550 --> 00:03:07,870
Say a twelve inch costs twelve dollars and

94
00:03:07,870 --> 00:03:09,790
an eighteen inch costs twenty.

95
00:03:09,790 --> 00:03:11,870
Two small ones cost twenty four dollars

96
00:03:12,030 --> 00:03:14,190
for two hundred twenty six square inches.

97
00:03:14,190 --> 00:03:16,350
That's about eleven cents per square inch.

98
00:03:16,350 --> 00:03:18,590
The big one costs about eight cents.

99
00:03:18,590 --> 00:03:20,670
At these prices, the eighteen inch is the

100
00:03:20,670 --> 00:03:22,350
better deal per square inch.

101
00:03:22,350 --> 00:03:25,150
The two small pizzas do win one thing:

102
00:03:25,150 --> 00:03:27,550
outer edge. The edge of a pizza is its

103
00:03:27,550 --> 00:03:29,710
circumference, pi times d.

104
00:03:29,710 --> 00:03:31,790
That grows in a straight line, not with

105
00:03:31,790 --> 00:03:34,270
the square. The two twelve inch pizzas

106
00:03:34,270 --> 00:03:36,030
have about seventy five inches of outer

107
00:03:36,030 --> 00:03:37,860
edge. The eighteen inch has about fifty

108
00:03:37,870 --> 00:03:39,310
six and a half.

109
00:03:39,310 --> 00:03:41,710
So the pair gives you a third more outer

110
00:03:41,710 --> 00:03:44,030
edge. How much actual crust that means

111
00:03:44,190 --> 00:03:46,590
depends on the rim's width and thickness.

112
00:03:46,590 --> 00:03:48,830
Now swap the pizza for a pipe.

113
00:03:48,830 --> 00:03:50,990
Water flows through the circle inside it,

114
00:03:50,990 --> 00:03:53,710
so what matters is the inside diameter.

115
00:03:53,710 --> 00:03:56,110
One pipe with a two inch inside diameter

116
00:03:56,110 --> 00:03:58,350
has twice the opening area of two pipes

117
00:03:58,350 --> 00:04:00,270
with one inch inside diameters.

118
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:02,420
At the same average water speed, the two

119
00:04:02,580 --> 00:04:04,660
inch opening passes twice as much water

120
00:04:04,660 --> 00:04:06,980
per second as the two one inch openings

121
00:04:06,980 --> 00:04:09,700
combined. Double a pipe's inside diameter,

122
00:04:09,700 --> 00:04:12,420
and the opening's area grows four times.

123
00:04:12,420 --> 00:04:14,500
That's why you can't size pipes by adding

124
00:04:14,500 --> 00:04:15,780
up diameters.

125
00:04:15,940 --> 00:04:18,340
Electrical wires follow the same rule.

126
00:04:18,340 --> 00:04:21,140
A wire's resistance is rho L over A.

127
00:04:21,140 --> 00:04:23,620
Rho depends on the metal, L is the length,

128
00:04:23,620 --> 00:04:25,780
and A is the cross section area of the

129
00:04:25,780 --> 00:04:27,780
conductor itself, the metal, not the

130
00:04:27,780 --> 00:04:30,100
insulation. For round conductors of the

131
00:04:30,100 --> 00:04:32,100
same material, length, and temperature,

132
00:04:32,100 --> 00:04:34,340
doubling the conductor diameter makes that

133
00:04:34,340 --> 00:04:36,500
area four times bigger, and cuts its

134
00:04:36,500 --> 00:04:38,020
resistance to one quarter.

135
00:04:38,020 --> 00:04:39,780
Electric stoves draw more current than

136
00:04:39,780 --> 00:04:41,700
lamps, so they typically use larger

137
00:04:41,700 --> 00:04:42,900
conductors.

138
00:04:42,900 --> 00:04:44,420
Bolts work the same way.

139
00:04:44,420 --> 00:04:46,660
When a bolt is pulled, the load spreads

140
00:04:46,660 --> 00:04:48,020
over its cross section.

141
00:04:48,020 --> 00:04:50,180
Take the smooth, unthreaded shank, since

142
00:04:50,180 --> 00:04:52,100
the threaded part has its own, smaller

143
00:04:52,100 --> 00:04:54,580
stress area. A three quarter inch bolt is

144
00:04:54,580 --> 00:04:56,260
one and a half times wider than a half

145
00:04:56,340 --> 00:04:58,550
inch bolt. So it has two and a quarter

146
00:04:58,550 --> 00:05:00,550
times the unthreaded shank area.

147
00:05:00,550 --> 00:05:02,390
At the same average tensile stress in the

148
00:05:02,390 --> 00:05:04,310
shank, that corresponds to two and a

149
00:05:04,390 --> 00:05:06,070
quarter times the pulling force.

150
00:05:06,070 --> 00:05:07,110
Sound familiar?

151
00:05:07,110 --> 00:05:09,030
It's the pizza ratio again.

152
00:05:09,030 --> 00:05:10,950
So here's what to remember.

153
00:05:10,950 --> 00:05:13,190
Area grows with the square of the

154
00:05:13,190 --> 00:05:15,670
diameter. Double the width, and you get

155
00:05:15,670 --> 00:05:17,190
four times the area.

156
00:05:17,190 --> 00:05:19,110
One and a half times the width gives two

157
00:05:19,270 --> 00:05:20,870
and a quarter times the area.

158
00:05:20,870 --> 00:05:22,870
And when you compare circles, compare

159
00:05:23,030 --> 00:05:24,790
areas, not diameters.

160
00:05:24,790 --> 00:05:26,710
If you're choosing by surface area, take

161
00:05:26,710 --> 00:05:28,070
the eighteen inch.

162
00:05:28,070 --> 00:05:30,070
If you enjoyed this, please give it a like

163
00:05:30,070 --> 00:05:31,590
and subscribe for more everyday

164
00:05:31,590 --> 00:05:33,430
engineering. Thanks for watching!
